[#4471](/kb/incidents/4471) was merged on the subject line ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject))
and marked known: one bug, one fix queued. Read by tenant, by the way each report came in and by what
its body says, it holds more than one problem, and each needs its own fix. Each now has a ticket.

<ProblemTable ticket={4471} />

## How to tell them apart

**`parser`.** The shared parser reads every date month first, and every tenant on file writes the day
first, so day and month swap. The bodies say it plainly: the booked date and the date on the invite
are the same two numbers the other way round. It comes in through the app, by email and through
booking-v2's form. The queued fix is for this one.

**`hint`.** Booking-v3's form prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field. People type what the hint
tells them, month first, and the form reads the field the tenant's way, day first. The symptom is the
same swap, but the code at fault is the form, not the parser: fixing the parser leaves it as it is. It
only comes in through booking-v3's form.

**`one-day`.** The date moves back by one day, or two people see two days for the same meeting
("Client in Lisbon got Tuesday. Client in Toronto got Monday."). A month-first parser swaps day and
month; it never moves a date by one day. This looks like a date-only value passing through a time
zone. The desk noted these reports as one-day moves and files them under `parser` by tenant, so they
are counted there too, the way the desk counts: footnoted where they are filed.

## Since then

Engineering closed #4471: `parser` is fixed, and `hint` won't be, because booking-v3's form is retired.
The update does not name the one-day moves. The desk files them under `parser`, so they close with it,
and the table above shows each state. If dates still move by one day after the parser fix, that is the
time-zone problem their ticket describes, and it needs a new ticket.

<Callout kind="warn">
Merging on the subject line cannot see any of this: the same subject lines come in under different
problems, and nobody reads the body. Decision 0001 needs a new record that replaces it: merge on cause
(tenant, way in, what the body shows), not on subject.
</Callout>

## What this page counts

Every number above is computed when the page renders, from `reports-4471.json` (one row per report id),
the tenant directory and `desk-notes.json`, with the desk's own rules. The logic is in
`src/lib/kb/problems.ts`: every report under its cause by `causeOf` from `causes.ts`, and the desk's
`oneDayMove` notes for `one-day`, still counted where they are filed. The tickets are listed in
`src/lib/data/split-4471.json`, and the engineering update in `src/lib/data/engineering-4471.json`.

